// For two integers a and b in the range [c - buffer_size, c), if a != b, then
// a % buffer_size != b % buffer_size, assuming buffer_size > 0.
// 
// Since i != cur_idx and both are in [post.tail - post.buffer_size, post.tail),
// we have log_entry_idx(i, pre.buffer_size) != log_entry_idx(cur_idx, pre.buffer_size).
// 
// Therefore, post.alive_bits[log_entry_idx(i, pre.buffer_size)] == pre.alive_bits[log_entry_idx(i, pre.buffer_size)],
// which means log_entry_is_alive(post.alive_bits, i, post.buffer_size) == log_entry_is_alive(pre.alive_bits, i, pre.buffer_size).

