    // Both i and cur_idx are in the range [post.tail - post.buffer_size, post.tail)
    // and i != cur_idx as int.
    // We need to show that (i % pre.buffer_size as int) != (cur_idx as int % pre.buffer_size as int).
    // 
    // Since both values are in the range [post.tail - post.buffer_size, post.tail), and they are different,
    // their modulo with respect to pre.buffer_size must also be different.
    // This is a property of modular arithmetic: if two integers differ by a non-zero multiple of n,
    // then their remainders modulo n are different.
    // But since both are in a range of size pre.buffer_size, their difference cannot be a multiple of pre.buffer_size
